WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.417
(voices murmuring)

00:00:04.870 --> 00:00:06.980
- [Caitlin] Using Bitcoin to buy clothes,

00:00:06.980 --> 00:00:10.680
snacks, even the daily
newspaper instead of US dollars

00:00:10.680 --> 00:00:13.430
is now an option to the
people in El Salvador

00:00:13.430 --> 00:00:15.510
as the country becomes
the first in the world

00:00:15.510 --> 00:00:18.613
to adopt the volatile crypto
as its national currency.

00:00:19.730 --> 00:00:21.950
It's a big test for
Bitcoin in the real world,

00:00:21.950 --> 00:00:23.680
and for Salvadorans.

00:00:23.680 --> 00:00:24.930
To get them started,

00:00:24.930 --> 00:00:27.100
the government is giving $30 to people

00:00:27.100 --> 00:00:29.560
who sign up to an e-wallet called Chivo,

00:00:29.560 --> 00:00:31.490
which allows for the automatic conversion

00:00:31.490 --> 00:00:33.913
of dollars to Bitcoin and vice versa.

00:00:35.080 --> 00:00:37.940
While some businesses welcome
this crypto experiment,

00:00:37.940 --> 00:00:40.090
80% of Salvadorians have little

00:00:40.090 --> 00:00:41.900
or no confidence in Bitcoin.

00:00:41.900 --> 00:00:44.690
And some have opposed the move.

00:00:44.690 --> 00:00:48.700
- One big reason is because
people don't want their wages

00:00:48.700 --> 00:00:50.600
to be denominated in Bitcoin.

00:00:50.600 --> 00:00:53.810
It's related to the sharp fluctuations

00:00:53.810 --> 00:00:55.800
in value that Bitcoin has.

00:00:55.800 --> 00:00:58.290
Also, a lot of people
think that El Salvador

00:00:58.290 --> 00:01:01.520
is not really prepared
for this type of adoption.

00:01:01.520 --> 00:01:04.400
A lot of people don't have smartphones,

00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:07.771
and if they do, they
don't have data plans.

00:01:07.771 --> 00:01:09.810
(people clapping)

00:01:09.810 --> 00:01:11.490
- And I worked really hard,

00:01:11.490 --> 00:01:14.320
and I lived there, and I
got to know the community,

00:01:14.320 --> 00:01:15.730
and I made friends that I hope

00:01:15.730 --> 00:01:17.280
will be at my wedding some day.

00:01:18.650 --> 00:01:21.560
And so with all that being said,

00:01:21.560 --> 00:01:22.963
I'd like to invite.

00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:26.170
- [Caitlin] El Salvador's
president announced the plan

00:01:26.170 --> 00:01:29.530
in June, making a surprise
appearance via video link

00:01:29.530 --> 00:01:32.670
at a Bitcoin conference
being held in Miami.

00:01:32.670 --> 00:01:34.490
- In the short-term,
this will generate jobs

00:01:34.490 --> 00:01:36.150
and help provide financial inclusion

00:01:36.150 --> 00:01:38.900
to thousands outside the formal economy.

00:01:38.900 --> 00:01:40.420
- [Caitlin] President Bukele has said

00:01:40.420 --> 00:01:43.209
that adopting Bitcoin
will, among other things,

00:01:43.209 --> 00:01:45.180
attract foreign investment

00:01:45.180 --> 00:01:47.850
and foster cheaper financial services.

00:01:47.850 --> 00:01:49.440
But it also risks wrecking

00:01:49.440 --> 00:01:52.483
El Salvador's $26 billion economy.

00:01:53.510 --> 00:01:55.590
Bitcoin is known for its big swings

00:01:55.590 --> 00:01:58.250
with huge sell-offs that
can be triggered by a tweet.

00:01:58.250 --> 00:02:00.760
And its decentralized
system opens the doors

00:02:00.760 --> 00:02:03.280
to anonymous and illicit transactions,

00:02:03.280 --> 00:02:06.553
like money laundering or ransom
payments, economists say.

00:02:07.750 --> 00:02:09.980
The government's plan has sparked protests

00:02:09.980 --> 00:02:13.025
in the impoverished
Central American nation.

00:02:13.025 --> 00:02:14.790
(shouting in foreign language)

00:02:14.790 --> 00:02:18.470
- The law was passed in a matter of hours

00:02:18.470 --> 00:02:20.903
without discussion with stakeholders.

00:02:22.460 --> 00:02:25.010
The private sector was never consulted.

00:02:25.010 --> 00:02:27.500
The same goes for labor unions

00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:30.310
or other segments of society.

00:02:30.310 --> 00:02:33.320
So it was, in a way, imposed,

00:02:33.320 --> 00:02:35.000
and this comes at a time

00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:39.380
when El Salvador is facing
some economic headwinds.

00:02:39.380 --> 00:02:42.490
They have a very
significant budget deficit.

00:02:42.490 --> 00:02:43.350
They are in talks

00:02:43.350 --> 00:02:46.000
with the International Monetary Fund

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:50.683
to get a financial aid
package of 1.3 billion.

00:02:52.950 --> 00:02:54.950
- [Caitlin] El Salvador's Finance Minister

00:02:54.950 --> 00:02:57.038
said he doesn't expect
Bitcoin's volatility

00:02:57.038 --> 00:02:58.810
to pose a problem,

00:02:58.810 --> 00:03:00.620
and that the instant convertibility

00:03:00.620 --> 00:03:03.080
of Bitcoin to dollars via Chivo

00:03:03.080 --> 00:03:04.760
is likely to be sufficient.

00:03:04.760 --> 00:03:06.897
Financial institutions
will also be required

00:03:06.897 --> 00:03:10.303
to alert customers of
Bitcoin's volatility.

00:03:11.420 --> 00:03:15.460
Bitcoin is currently trading
at around $50,000 each.

00:03:15.460 --> 00:03:18.070
Bitcoin's adoption as
legal tender in El Salvador

00:03:18.070 --> 00:03:20.710
is unprecedented, and this experiment

00:03:20.710 --> 00:03:22.182
is going to be closely monitored

00:03:22.182 --> 00:03:25.800
by crypto advocates, global
financial institutions,

00:03:25.800 --> 00:03:27.590
and governments around the world

00:03:27.590 --> 00:03:30.310
to see how it works, how effective it is,

00:03:30.310 --> 00:03:32.297
and what the consequences could be.

00:03:32.297 --> 00:03:37.297
(food frying)
(dramatic music)

